BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Once Upon a Time in China with Jet Li
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260508
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019d6e27-5fdb-a93e-4e67-0cdc0ff3e52f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Actor Jet Li\n\nFriday\, May 8\, 2026\n\nLocation: 
 Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 14m\n\n1991 | 134 min | H
 ong Kong | Color | Scope | Cantonese\, English and French with English sub
 titles | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Tsui Hark \nWRITTEN BY: Tsui Hark\,
  Yuen Kai-Chi\, Leung Yiu-Ming\, Tang Bik-Yin \nWITH: Jet Li\, Rosamund Kw
 an\, Yuen Biao\, Jacky Cheung\n\nType: Screenings\n\nMartial arts master a
 nd Hong Kong film icon Jet Li stars as Chinese folk hero Wong Fei-Hung in 
 Tsui Hark’s wuxia (a genre focusing on martial artists in ancient China 
 with fantastical elements) epic. In the late 19th century\, as Western imp
 erialists threaten Chinese sovereignty\, Wong uses his kung fu mastery to 
 train a militia to protect a threatened land and national identity. Full o
 f social and political commentary\, punctuated by jaw-dropping action scen
 es\, and featuring dazzling choreography and wirework showcasing Li’s re
 markable acrobatics\, the film launched Li as an international action supe
 rstar and was followed by five sequels\, as well as a TV series. \nBefore 
 the screening\, Li will be signing copies of his new book\, Beyond Life an
 d Death: The Way of True Freedom\, at the Academy Museum Store. The signin
 g is a separately ticketed event.\nCo-presented by Gold House.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/once-upon-a-time-in-c
 hina-with-jet-li-019d6e27-5fdb-a93e-4e67-0cdc0ff3e52f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Red Beard (Akahige) in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260508
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019c0656-595b-c83a-0c1b-d2f649f0a9fb@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, May 8\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pi
 ctures\n\nRuntime: 2h 45m\n\n1965 | 165 min. | Japan | Black-and-White | J
 apanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 35mm. \nDIRECTED BY: Akira Ku
 rosawa\nWRITTEN BY: Akira Kurosawa\, Hideo Oguni\, Ryuzo Kikushima\, Masat
 o Ide \nBASED ON A STORY BY: Shugoro Yamamoto \nWITH: Toshiro Mifune\, Yu
 zo Kayama\, Yoshio Tsuchiya\, Tatsuyoshi Ehara\n\nType: Screenings\n\nKuro
 sawa and Toshiro Mifune’s grand marathon of collaborations\, which yield
 ed numerous masterpieces\, faces its finish line with a three-hour explora
 tion of moral values and existential contemplation of humankind\, led by a
 nother heartfelt performance by Mifune as a humble and compassionate clini
 c director\, aka Red Beard. He\, welcomes a young doctor\, Yasumoto (Yuzo 
 Kayama)\, into his small-town practice\, only to discover that his protég
 é is arrogant\, blinded by ambition\, and reluctant to serve patients wit
 h low social standing. Kurosawa examines humanity with a thoughtful gaze\,
  gently excavating the innate goodness of humankind through lessons from b
 oth life and death.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/red-beard-019c0656-59
 5b-c83a-0c1b-d2f649f0a9fb
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beyond Life and Death: The Way of True Freedom Book Signing with A
 uthor Jet Li
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260508
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019d8d7c-a646-6ded-bbfc-49a4daf4d7fd@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Book Signings
DESCRIPTION:Martial arts legend and international movie star Jet Li signs 
 copies of his insightful new book.\n\nFriday\, May 8\, 2026\n\nLocation: A
 cademy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nType: Book Signings\n\nMartial arts ch
 ampion and international movie star Jet Li signs copies of his insightful 
 new book at the Academy Museum Store.\nAbout the author\nJet Li is an inte
 rnationally acclaimed martial artist\, actor\, and philanthropist. After r
 ising to fame as a five-time national wushu champion and starring in Shaol
 in Temple\, he became a global icon through films such as Hero (2002)\, Fe
 arless (2006)\, and Romeo Must Die (2000). Following a near-death experien
 ce in the 2004 tsunami\, he founded the One Foundation to promote philanth
 ropy and community giving. A student of Tibetan Buddhism for 30 years\, Li
  brings a lifetime of discipline\, reflection\, and spiritual insight to t
 his deeply personal book.\nAbout the book \nMartial arts legend and intern
 ational movie star Jet Li distills 10 powerful insights from his iconic ca
 reer\, his personal life and philosophies\, and his 30-year Buddhist pract
 ice. Jet Li’s story defies legend. Born into extreme hardship\, he fough
 t his way to become the youngest national martial arts champion in Chinese
  history at 12\, dominating opponents twice his size. He then became one o
 f the first internationally renowned movie stars from China with films inc
 luding Once Upon a Time in China (1991)\, Hero\, and Fearless. These films
  redefined martial arts for the modern world\, making him a household name
 . But behind the glory lay a deeper battle: a search for meaning beyond fa
 me\, fortune\, and physical skill. After a near-death encounter in the 200
 4 tsunami\, Li turned inward\, deepening his study of Tibetan Buddhism and
  dedicating his life to philanthropy\, though he was at the height of his 
 Hollywood career. For the very first time\, Li shares the 10 insights that
  have guided his life\, in which anyone can find wisdom\, guidance\, and p
 ower\, including: \nLife is movement\nThe secret to self-defense\nSeparate
  the bitterness from the pain\nBe a grandson to the world\, and\nLearn fro
 m everyone\nLi invites readers to share his interior life\, to hear untold
  stories from his martial arts and film career\, and to meditate with him 
 on the nature of spiritual awakening. If you look deeply\, you can see Li
 ’s life philosophy in many of his movies\, and in Beyond Life and Death\
 , he fully links his own story and spiritual journey with 10 actionable in
 sights that anyone can apply to live a healthy and happy life.\nAfter the 
 signing\, in a separately ticketed event\, Li will host a screening of his
  1991 film Once Upon a Time in China.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/beyond-life-and-death
 -the-way-of-true-freedom-book-signing-with-author-jet-li-019d8d7c-a646-6de
 d-bbfc-49a4daf4d7fd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bearing Witness: 10 Films by Kevin Jerome Everson
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260510
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019db266-9028-6725-d4cc-7e6cacb94373@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: filmmaker Kevin Jerome Everson\n\nSaturday\, May 9\
 , 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 3m\n\nDo
 uble Feature at the Sunset Drive-In  \n2024 | 3 min. | USA | Color | Soun
 d | Not Rated | Digital  \nWITH: Tre’Zhan Gamble  \n*** \nThe I and S
  of Lives  \n2021 | 7 min. | USA | Color | Sound | Not Rated | Digital  \
 nWITH: Jahleel Gardner\n***\nCondor  \n2019 | 8 min. | USA | Black-and-Wh
 ite | Sound | Not Rated | Digital  \n \n***\nIFO  \n2017 | 10 min. | US
 A | Black-and-White | English | Not Rated | Digital  \nWITH: Albert Thoma
 s. Elijah Bailey Harris\, Saveon Moore\, Carmenita Higginbotham\, Matilda 
 Washington \n***\nPlaying Dead  \n2008 | 2 min. | USA | Color | English |
  Not Rated | Digital  \n***\nEmergency Needs \n2007 | 7 min | USA | Color
  | English | Not Rated | Digital  \nWITH: Mayor Carl B. Stokes\, Esosa Edo
 somwan \n***\nThe Wood Thrush and the Bobwhite Quail  \n2025 | 5 min. | U
 SA | Color | Sound | Not Rated | Digital  \nWITH: Derek Stewart\, Isaac C
 rayton\, Derrick Hardaway  \n***\nHazel (dual)  \n2023 | 12 min. | USA |
  Black-and-White | Sound | Not Rated | Digital  \nWITH: Ricky Goldman \n*
 **\nMusic from the Edge of the Allegheny Plateau  \n2019 | 7 min. | USA |
  Color | English | Not Rated | Digital  \nWITH: Sidney Brown Jr.\, Jamie 
 Hillard\, Taj Torrence\, Matilda Washington \n***\nTraveling Shoes \n2019
  | 7 min. | USA | Black-and-White | English | Not Rated | Digital\nWITH: S
 idney Brown Sr.\, Robert Whitfield\, Matilda Washington\, Kimberly Knox\n\
 nType: Screenings\n\nBorn in Mansfield\, Ohio\, and now living and working
  in Charlottesville\, Virginia\, Kevin Jerome Everson is the Commonwealth 
 and Ruffin Foundation Distinguished Professor of Studio Art\, Director of 
 Studio Arts\, University of Virginia. Everson's art practice encompasses p
 rintmaking\, sculpture\, photography\, and film\, including 13 features an
 d more than 300 solo and collaborative shorts. \nAcross these 10 short fil
 ms\, which represent just a fraction of 20 years of cinematic output and e
 xploration\, Everson’s persistent interest in looking is interwoven with
  his unmatched sense of musicality. From revisiting film history at an Ohi
 o drive-in (Double Feature at the Sunset Drive-In\, 2024) to reclaiming a 
 dismantled memorial (The I and S of Lives\, 2021)\, Everson “creates a w
 ide array of distilled interpretations of aspects of Black life in the USA
 \, in part producing an archive of lived experiences that have been erased
  in dominant culture” (Adam Hyman). This program looks to the sky to ima
 gine life far beyond our own (IFO\, 2017) as well as existences just withi
 n reach (The Wood Thrush and the Bobwhite Quail\, 2025)\, building a bridg
 e between the visual and sonic experiences of being present\, “eras[ing]
  the line between staging and verité” (Hyman). \nThe Los Angeles Filmfo
 rum presents a different program with Everson on Tuesday\, May 12\, at 222
 0 Arts + Archives.\nSpecial Thanks to Madeleine Molyneaux\, Adam Hyman\, a
 nd Los Angeles Filmforum. \nFilms appear courtesy the artist\; trilobite-a
 rts DAC\; Picture Palace Pictures. All films directed by Kevin Jerome Ever
 son.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/bearing-witness-ten-f
 ilms-by-kevin-jerome-everson-019db266-9028-6725-d4cc-7e6cacb94373
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grand Guignol Silent Shorts
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260510
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019d98b2-6ee0-f832-9f24-2280035ed5e7@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Bret Berg\, head of theatrical\, AGFA\n\nSaturday\,
  May 9\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1
 h 20m\n\n1898-1921 | 80 min. | USA/UK/France | Black-and-White | Silent | 
 Not Rated | 4K DCP\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDown a late-19th-century back al
 ley in Paris’s seedy Pigalle district\, a former-chapel- turned-performa
 nce space became a theatrical institution forged in naturalism\, controver
 sy and grisly spectacle. By the early 1920s\, pioneering filmmakers had be
 gun to adapt Grand Guignol vignettes for a slate of intense one-reelers dr
 ipping with psychological terror. These were seen as milestones in the evo
 lution of the horror genre before it had a name. \nMore than six decades s
 ince its final performance\, the Grand Guignol remains one of the most wil
 dly misunderstood and profoundly influential traditions in entertainment h
 istory. From horror films to tabloid journalism\, avant-garde theater to t
 he true-crime genre\, France’s Theater of Horrors continues to impact po
 pular culture worldwide. \nToday’s program highlights the most impactful
  of these shorts\, including several by prolific British filmmaker Fred Pa
 ul\, whose undiscovered work was recently unveiled at the British Film Ins
 titute. This screening features brand-new 4K restorations by Severin Films
  with all-new music by David J (Bauhaus\, Love and Rockets) with Tony Gree
 n and LA-based silent score veteran Michael Mortilla. \nShorts included in
  the program:									 \nCutter of Heads\nThe Flat\nDelilah  \nWoman Misu
 nderstood \nThe Doll’s Revenge \nThe Jest \nThe Gentle Doctor \nThe A
 ntidote  \nFigures of Wax \nVoice from the Dead \nThis program is screeni
 ng as part of the Programmers’ Jam\, an annual gathering of repertory ex
 hibitors and distributors.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/grand-guignol-silent-
 shorts-019d98b2-6ee0-f832-9f24-2280035ed5e7
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ponyo
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260510
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019be21f-9378-34da-84cd-78300fe63dc9@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 9\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n2008 | 103 min. | Japan | Color | English (
 Dubbed) | Rated G | DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Hayao Miyazaki \nWITH: Cate
  Blanchett\, Noah Cyrus\, Matt Damon\, Tina Fey\n\nType: Screenings\n\nPon
 yo focuses on the friendship between 5-year-old Sosuke and a magical goldf
 ish named Brunhilde\, the young daughter of a sorcerer father and a sea-go
 ddess mother. After wandering away from her father’s four-flippered subm
 arine\, Brunhilde washes ashore and is discovered by the curious Sosuke. N
 ow renamed Ponyo\, her quick bond with Sosuke fuels her yearning to be a r
 eal girl\, and they shoulder the cost of what that might take together. Th
 e vibrant and colorful hand-drawn animations are a visual delight for audi
 ences of all ages\, as Hayao Miyazaki builds a world filled with magical g
 oldfish\, wizards\, and sea goddesses in this tale of how friendships can 
 blossom anywhere—even in the ocean’s depths.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/ponyo-019be21f-9378-3
 4da-84cd-78300fe63dc9
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Terms of Endearment in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T160000
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019be227-f630-7bc5-f8b7-e5be86b1f82f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, May 10\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of 
 Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 9m\n\n1983 | 129 min. | USA | Color | Engli
 sh | Rated PG | 35mm \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: James L. Brooks \nWITH: Debra 
 Winger\, Shirley MacLaine\, Jack Nicholson\, John Lithgow \nNew print cour
 tesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nVeteran TV writer
 -producer James L. Brooks made his feature directing debut with this hilar
 ious yet heartbreaking adaptation of the novel by Larry McMurtry (The Last
  Picture Show\, 1971)\, following the complicated relationship between a s
 trong-willed mother (Shirley MacLaine\, winning her only Oscar) and her da
 ughter (fellow Best Actress nominee Debra Winger). Jack Nicholson won his 
 second Oscar for his supporting role as a free-spirited astronaut who roma
 nces MacLaine\, with John Lithgow also nominated as Winger’s well-meanin
 g suitor. Another member of the top-notch cast\, chosen by Brooks and lege
 ndary casting directors Ellen Chenoweth and Juliet Taylor\, was Jeff Danie
 ls\, in his breakout role as Winger’s feckless husband. \nThe film also 
 earned three Oscars for Brooks himself—for Best Picture\, Directing\, an
 d his adapted screenplay.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/terms-of-endearment-0
 19be227-f630-7bc5-f8b7-e5be86b1f82f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Wages of Fear in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260511T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260511T163000
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019be23d-3b37-f09b-fc4c-081fba6522a3@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, May 11\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 35m\n\n1953 | 155 min. | France\, Italy 
 | Black-and-White | French with English subtitles | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nD
 IRECTED BY: Henri-Georges Clouzot \nWRITTEN BY: Henri-Georges Clouzot\, J
 érôme Géronimi \nWITH: Yves Montand\, Charles Vanel\, Peter van Eyck\, 
 Folco Lulli\n\nType: Screenings\n\nWriter-director Henri-Georges Clouzot (
 Diabolique\, 1955) adapted Georges Arnaud’s 1950 novel for this intense 
 thriller\, which won the Golden Bear at the Berlin International Film Fest
 ival and the Palme d’Or at Cannes. Yves Montand plays Mario\, a playboy 
 stuck in a remote South American town. Down on his luck\, he joins three o
 ther desperate men in a death-defying task: driving two trucks loaded with
  nitroglycerine over treacherous mountain roads to put out an oil well fir
 e. Bong Joon Ho told an interviewer in 2020 that this was one of two films
  he saw when he was nine that inspired him to become a film director\; the
  other was Psycho (1960). William Friedkin remade the story in English in 
 1977 as Sorcerer.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/wages-of-fear-019be23
 d-3b37-f09b-fc4c-081fba6522a3
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rhapsody in August (Hachigatsu no kyoshikyoku) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260511T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260511T203000
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019d44de-c65c-92fc-1959-2d5c17be738a@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, May 11\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 38m\n\n1991 | 98 min | Japan | Color | J
 apanese with English subtitles | Rated PG | 35mm  \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: 
 Akira Kurosawa \nWITH: Sachiko Murase\, Hisashi Igawa\, Narumi Kayashima\
 , Tomoko Otakara \nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Sc
 reenings\n\nBased on Inside a Pot by distinguished female novelist Kiyoko 
 Murata\, Kurosawa’s penultimate film centers on widow Kane (Sachiko Mura
 se)\, whose husband was killed by the atomic bomb dropped by the Americans
  on Nagasaki. Now a grandmother\, Kane welcomes her grandchildren to her r
 ural home\, where the impact of her decades of silence becomes impossible 
 to ignore.\n“Making an antiwar picture isn’t a matter of re-creating b
 attle scenes\,” Kurosawa said in 1991. The director instead relies on th
 e sweltering summer heat and softly spoken observances to convey the impac
 ts of generational trauma caused by wartime tragedies. American actor Rich
 ard Gere\, who appears as one of Kane’s nephews\, agreed to make the pic
 ture on the modest condition that his name was not used to sell the film.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/rhapsody-in-august-ha
 chigatsu-no-kyoshikyoku-in-35-mm-019d44de-c65c-92fc-1959-2d5c17be738a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Wages of Fear in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T163000
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019be23e-2972-eb73-6f3d-405c6ec15392@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, May 13\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 35m\n\n1953 | 155 min. | France\, Ita
 ly | Black-and-White | French with English subtitles | Not Rated | 4K DCP 
 \nDIRECTED BY: Henri-Georges Clouzot \nWRITTEN BY: Henri-Georges Clouzot\,
  Jérôme Géronimi \nWITH: Yves Montand\, Charles Vanel\, Peter van Eyck\
 , Folco Lulli\n\nType: Screenings\n\nWriter-director Henri-Georges Clouzot
  (Diabolique\, 1955) adapted Georges Arnaud’s 1950 novel for this intens
 e thriller\, which won the Golden Bear at the Berlin International Film Fe
 stival and the Palme d’Or at Cannes. Yves Montand plays Mario\, a playbo
 y stuck in a remote South American town. Down on his luck\, he joins three
  other desperate men in a death-defying task: driving two trucks loaded wi
 th nitroglycerine over treacherous mountain roads to put out an oil well f
 ire. Bong Joon Ho told an interviewer in 2020 that this was one of two fil
 ms he saw when he was nine that inspired him to become a film director\; t
 he other was Psycho (1960). William Friedkin remade the story in English i
 n 1977 as Sorcerer.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/wages-of-fear-019be23
 e-2972-eb73-6f3d-405c6ec15392
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening of Short Films from Asian American Filmmakers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T223000
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019be210-a94b-d065-dfac-b8b273f32904@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Short Films Branch \nIn person: Academy Govern
 or Chris Tashima and filmmakers Andrew Ahn\, Nazrin Choudhury\, Jon M. Chu
 \, and Arthur Dong\n\nWednesday\, May 13\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Ac
 ademy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 6m\n\nBead Game \n1977 | 6 min
 . | Canada | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Ishu Patel \nSoar \nDIRECTED/W
 RITTEN BY: Alyce Tzue \n2014 | 7 min. | USA | Color | English \nWITH: Shir
 a Abergel\, Mason Welch \nSewing Woman \n1982 | 14 min. | USA | Black-and-
 White | English\nDIRECTED BY: Arthur Dong \nWRITTEN BY: Lorraine Dong \nWI
 TH: Lisa Lu \nNai Nai & Wài Pó \n2023 | 17 min. | USA | Color | English\
 , Mandarin \nDIRECTED BY: Sean Wang \nGwai Lo: The Little Foreigner \n2002
  | 12 min. | USA | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Jon M. Chu \nDol (First 
 Birthday) \n2011 | 12 min. | USA | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITEN BY: A
 ndrew Ahn \nWITH: Muki Grossberg\, Joshua Kwak\, James S.W. Lee\, Martin L
 ee \nNami \n2015 | 13 min. | USA | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: 
 Masami Kawai \nWITH: Kana Kawai \nWinning in America \n2021 | 10 min. | US
 A | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Amrita Singh \nWITH: Rithika Tu
 dmilla\, Ranjan Singh\, Shiney Simon\, Rahul Tudmilla\n\nType: Screenings\
 n\nThe Academy is celebrating Asian American\, Native Hawaiian\, and Pacif
 ic Islander Heritage month with this selection of short films featuring As
 ian American filmmakers and stories. The evening includes two animated fil
 ms\, Ishu Patel’s Oscar-nominated Bead Game (1977)\, and Soar (2014)\, f
 rom filmmaker Alyce Tzue. Arthur Dong’s Oscar-nominated documentary shor
 t\, Sewing Woman (1982)\, tells the life story of the filmmaker’s mother
 \, while Sean Wang (Dìdi) was nominated for his documentary Nai Nai & Wà
 i Pó (2023)\, depicting the close friendship of his elderly grandmothers.
  Jon M. Chu (Wicked\, 2024) won a DGA Student Film Award for his musical s
 hort Gwai Lo: The Little Foreigner (2002). Filmmaker Andrew Ahn (Fire Isla
 nd\, 2022) made his short film Dol (First Birthday\, 2011) partly as a way
  of coming out to his parents. Masami Kawai’s Nami (2015) depicts a day 
 in the life of a grieving widow in her journey across Los Angeles. In Amri
 ta Singh’s Winning in America (2021)\, a teenage girl faces the challeng
 es of a spelling bee and her coach father.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/an-evening-of-short-f
 ilms-from-asian-american-filmmakers-019be210-a94b-d065-dfac-b8b273f32904
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Night and the City in 35mm nitrate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T203000
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019c0651-3856-5dfc-6db8-c395e72fb72a@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, May 14\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 36m\n\n1950 | 96 min. | UK/USA | Black
 -and-White | English | Not Rated | 35mm nitrate \nDIRECTED BY: Jules Dassi
 n\nWRITTEN BY: Jo Eisinger\nWITH: Richard Widmark\, Gene Tierney\, Googie 
 Withers\, Hugh Marlowe \n35mm nitrate collection print courtesy of the UCL
 A Film & Television Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAmerican director Jule
 s Dassin’s British noir follows Harry (Richard Widmark)\, a small-time h
 ustler dreaming of dominating the wrestling racket. When he double-crosses
  London’s underworld\, his lies become a death warrant in the city’s m
 erciless alleys.\nShot in the UK while Dassin was fleeing persecution and 
 the Hollywood blacklist\, Night and the City is the first of several films
  he made abroad in Britain\, France\, and Greece. This rare original nitra
 te print is of the British release version of the film\, which runs six mi
 nutes longer than the US release and features alternate opening and closin
 g scenes as well as a score by prolific British composer Benjamin Frankel.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/night-and-the-city-in
 -35-mm-nitrate-019c0651-3856-5dfc-6db8-c395e72fb72a
END:VEVENT
