SUMMARY:Howl’s Moving Castle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T121500
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019be220-5fd1-2ac7-7ae3-ec50e4adf5b3@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 16\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 59m\n\n2004 | 119 min. | Japan | Color |
  English (Dubbed) | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Hayao Miyazaki\nW
 ITH: Jean Simmons\, Christian Bale\, Lauren Bacall\, Blythe Danner\n\nType
 : Screenings\n\nAn adaptation of Diana Wynne Jones’s fantasy novel of th
 e same name\, the Oscar-nominated Howl’s Moving Castle is a pitch-perfec
 t fairy tale about aging and war\, set in a dazzling steampunk world. When
  young hatmaker Sophie is transformed into a 90-year-old woman by the veng
 eful Witch of the Waste\, she seeks to break the curse with the help of th
 e enigmatic wizard Howl\, the fire demon Calcifer\, and the magical moving
  castle they inhabit.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/howls-moving-castle-0
 19be220-5fd1-2ac7-7ae3-ec50e4adf5b3
