BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dreams (Yume) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260529T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260529T213000
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019c0661-f193-f899-3028-5842d51ed060@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, May 29\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum 
 of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h\n\n1990 | 120 min. | Japan | Color | Jap
 anese with English subtitles | Rated PG | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Akira
  Kurosawa\nWITH: Akira Terao\, Mitsuko Baisho\, Toshie Negishi\, Mieko Har
 ada  \nNew print courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screening
 s\n\n“Any description of dreams in mere words cannot capture their expre
 ssive power.” \n—Akira Kurosawa\, 1993  \nInspired by a passage in a 
 novel by Fjodor Dostoevsky “where he talks about dreams and the fact tha
 t they express our deepest fears and greatest hopes\,” Dreams is a visua
 lly sumptuous entry in the latter half of the filmmaker’s career. Divide
 d into eight chapters reflecting dreams from Kurosawa’s childhood throug
 h his late seventies\, this impressionistic wonder was released\, appropri
 ately\, the year after the director received an Honorary Oscar from the Ac
 ademy “for cinematic accomplishments that have inspired\, delighted\, en
 riched\, and entertained worldwide audiences and influenced filmmakers thr
 oughout the world.”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/dreams-yume-in-35-mm-
 019c0661-f193-f899-3028-5842d51ed060
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Boy and the Heron
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T121500
DTSTAMP:20260510T084150Z
UID:019be220-9c0e-c24b-a8ce-9d4d515e0c35@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Accessible screening\n\nSaturday\, May 30\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nL
 ocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 4m\n\n2023 | 124
  min. | Japan | Color | English (Dubbed) | Rated PG-13 | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRI
 TTEN BY: Hayao Miyazaki\nWITH: Luca Padovan\, Robert Pattinson\, Christian
  Bale\, Gemma Chan\, Dave Bautista\n\nType: Screenings\n\nHayao Miyazaki
 ’s latest Oscar-winning feature is also his most autobiographical\, insp
 ired by Genzaburo Yoshino’s 1937 novel How Do You Live? (which is the Ja
 panese title for the film)\, and the effect World War II had on Miyazaki's
  childhood. The result is one of Miyazaki’s darkest and most mature film
 s. After losing his mother during the war\, Mahito and his father move to 
 the countryside for a fresh start. Still haunted by this loss and the rece
 nt disappearance of his new stepmom\, Mahito is lured to an ancient tower 
 by a gray heron and ends up in a world where the distinction between the l
 iving and the dead disappears. Guided by the heron\, he must battle his gr
 ief and learn that he has the capability to create a better world.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-boy-and-the-heron
 -019be220-9c0e-c24b-a8ce-9d4d515e0c35
END:VEVENT
